  "label": "The person in the image is mapped as the one experiencing extreme frustration over a gas bill",
  "description": "The visual entity 'Adolf_Hitler' is mapped onto the textual entity 'text_chunk' to represent the exaggerated emotional state of frustration one feels when seeing a gas bill. The image of Hitler, known for his intense rage, is used to symbolize the overwhelming and absurdly intense reaction to a mundane financial expense. This mapping is established through the juxtaposition of the visual pose (raised fist, shouting) with the text 'when you see the gas bill', creating an analogical equivalence between the historical figure's rage and the modern person's frustration.",
